# Order Service — end-to-end request script (ORD-14, D3 Part 1.3)
#
# One errand from creation to the courier's payment, a second one cancelled, and the refusals in
# between: accepting your own errand, an unrelated student acting, a stale version, and confirming
# twice. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" and the IntelliJ HTTP Client (both read `# @name` and
# `{{name.response.body.field}}`).
#
# Prerequisites: bring the stack up first, from the repo root:
#     docker compose up --build
#   user-service → :3001, supplier-service → :3002, order-service → :3003, credit-service → :3004.
#
# Run the requests in order: each block reuses tokens and IDs from the ones before. Three students are
# registered and activated here through the dev mailbox: a requester, a courier, and a bystander
# with no part in the errand. Re-running against the same database gets 409 on register; reset the
# database (`docker compose down -v`) or change the three emails.
#
# Two steps wait on the Credit Service, which answers by message: a new student's wallet (10 credits)
# and an errand's reservation. If a step says "status OPEN" and you see PENDING_CREDIT, send it
# again after a moment.

@userBase = http://localhost:3001
@orderBase = http://localhost:3003
@creditBase = http://localhost:3004

@password = Student-Passw0rd-01
@requesterEmail = ord14.requester@u.nus.edu
@courierEmail = ord14.courier@u.nus.edu
@bystanderEmail = ord14.bystander@u.nus.edu

# "Cafe+ Robot Cafe", Central Library: a seeded supplier. Seeded IDs are stable across fresh stacks.
@supplierId = 2c6eb5e4-037e-525a-bebe-063fe1fcabe4

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1 · Three students
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1a · Register the requester — expect 201
POST {{userBase}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{requesterEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "ORD-14 Requester" }

### 1b · Read the requester's activation token from the dev mailbox
# @name requesterMail
GET {{userBase}}/dev/mailbox?to={{requesterEmail}}

### 1c · Activate the requester — expect 200
POST {{userBase}}/auth/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{requesterMail.response.body.token}}" }

### 1d · Requester login — expect 200
# @name requesterLogin
POST {{userBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{requesterEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@requester = {{requesterLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1e · Register the courier — expect 201
POST {{userBase}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{courierEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "ORD-14 Courier" }

### 1f · Read the courier's activation token
# @name courierMail
GET {{userBase}}/dev/mailbox?to={{courierEmail}}

### 1g · Activate the courier — expect 200
POST {{userBase}}/auth/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{courierMail.response.body.token}}" }

### 1h · Courier login — expect 200
# @name courierLogin
POST {{userBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{courierEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@courier = {{courierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1i · Register the bystander — expect 201
POST {{userBase}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{bystanderEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "ORD-14 Bystander" }

### 1j · Read the bystander's activation token
# @name bystanderMail
GET {{userBase}}/dev/mailbox?to={{bystanderEmail}}

### 1k · Activate the bystander — expect 200
POST {{userBase}}/auth/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{bystanderMail.response.body.token}}" }

### 1l · Bystander login — expect 200
# @name bystanderLogin
POST {{userBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{bystanderEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@bystander = {{bystanderLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1m · The requester's wallet: 10 credits on activation — expect 200, available 10
GET {{creditBase}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 1n · The courier's wallet — expect 200, available 10
GET {{creditBase}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2 · Create an errand and find it
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2a · The requester posts an errand with a 2-credit reward — expect 201, status PENDING_CREDIT
# @name createErrand
POST {{orderBase}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ord14-errand-1

{
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "items": [{ "name": "Iced latte", "quantity": 1, "note": "Oat milk, less ice" }],
  "deliveryZone": "COM2 Level 1",
  "deliveryInstructions": "Leave it on the bench outside SR1 and message me",
  "reward": 2
}

###
@errand = {{createErrand.response.body.orderId}}

### 2b · The requester's private view, once Credit has reserved the reward — expect 200, status OPEN
# Version 2. The requester's wallet now shows 8 available and 2 reserved.
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}?view=private
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 2c · Couriers list open errands: public fields only, no instructions or item notes — expect 200
GET {{orderBase}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}

### 2d · The same errand to a courier who has not accepted it: the public view — expect 200
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}

### 2e · Refused: the requester accepts their own errand — expect 403, code SELF_ACCEPTANCE_FORBIDDEN
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 2 }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3 · Deliver it
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3a · The courier accepts, sending the version they saw — expect 201, status ACCEPTED
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 2 }

### 3b · Refused: the bystander accepts too late — expect 409, code ORDER_NOT_OPEN
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{bystander}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 2 }

### 3c · Refused: the bystander, who has no part in it, records pickup — expect 403, code ACTION_FORBIDDEN
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{bystander}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 3 }

### 3d · The courier records pickup — expect 200, status PICKED_UP
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 3 }

### 3e · Refused: the courier records delivery with a stale version — expect 409, code ORDER_CHANGED
# The error carries the current status and version (PICKED_UP, 4) to retry with.
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 3 }

### 3f · The courier records delivery — expect 200, status DELIVERED
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 4 }

### 3g · The requester confirms receipt — expect 200, status COMPLETION_PENDING_CREDIT
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/confirm-receipt
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 5 }

### 3h · Refused: the requester confirms again — expect 409, code INVALID_ORDER_STATE
# Nothing is requested a second time, so the courier is paid once.
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/confirm-receipt
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 6 }

### 3i · Once Credit has transferred the reward — expect 200, status COMPLETED
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}?view=private
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 3j · The receipt — expect 200
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/receipt
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 3k · Every change, in order, with who made it — expect 200
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{errand}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 3l · The courier was paid: 10 + 2 — expect 200, available 12
GET {{creditBase}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4 · Cancel a second errand
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4a · The requester posts another errand — expect 201, status PENDING_CREDIT
# @name secondErrand
POST {{orderBase}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ord14-errand-2

{
  "supplierId": "{{supplierId}}",
  "items": [{ "name": "Croissant", "quantity": 2 }],
  "deliveryZone": "COM2 Level 1",
  "deliveryInstructions": "Same bench as before",
  "reward": 3
}

###
@second = {{secondErrand.response.body.orderId}}

### 4b · Once the reward is reserved — expect 200, status OPEN
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{second}}?view=private
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 4c · Refused: the courier cancels someone else's errand — expect 403, code ACTION_FORBIDDEN
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{second}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{courier}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 2 }

### 4d · The requester cancels — expect 200, status RELEASE_PENDING_CREDIT
POST {{orderBase}}/orders/{{second}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedVersion": 2 }

### 4e · Once Credit has returned the reward — expect 200, status CANCELLED
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/{{second}}?view=private
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 4f · The requester paid 2 for the first errand and got the second's 3 back — expect 200, available 8
GET {{creditBase}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}

### 4g · Both errands, with the requester's role on each — expect 200
GET {{orderBase}}/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{requester}}
